<title>USA: Fieldcrest sued for patent infringement.</title>
<headline>Fieldcrest sued for patent infringement.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>A start-up home decorating manufacturer on Monday filed a patent infringement suit against Fieldcrest Cannon Inc, alleging that the textile giant is using the smaller company's information to make a grip for holding slipcovers.</p>
<p>In the lawsuit, filed in Manhattan federal court, New York-based PRescient Partners LP accused Fieldcrest and its Sure Fit Inc unit of patent infringement, misappropriation of trade secrets and false advertising.</p>
<p>The suit seeks unspecified damages and the recall and destruction of the allegedly infringing grips.</p>
</text>
